======================================================================
PLAN FOR APPROVAL
======================================================================
## Re-key the saddle-parity (gamma>1) far-field/ppGO admission predicate so the transverse (hard-axis) cone is served analytically instead of falling through to slow live quadrature. Root cause: the single-source-of-truth serve gate `_saddle_farfield_analytic_serves` (likelihood.py ~536-590) uses a scalar isotropic gauge `rho=|y|/caustic_reach >= _SADDLE_FARFIELD_RHO_FLOOR(2.0)` that underestimates distance to the TWO disconnected deltoid lobes, so a source far from both lobes (true nearest-caustic distance up to ~2.5) is wrongly refused. Fix: replace the rho accuracy term with a directional `eta = nearest_caustic_point(...).distance >= _SADDLE_ETA_FLOOR(0.15)` term (Leg A), and make the w-resolution leg (Leg B) treat symmetry-tied mirror pairs (delta_tau<=tie_eps) as non-resolving. Serve = (A AND B). SCOPE CORRECTION from Professor consultation: the CONNECTING region (origin->deltoid, rho<0.5, mirror pair with delta_tau==0) CANNOT be served in this build — the certified ppGO map is keyed on the same scalar rho and hard-refuses saddle rho<1 cells, so no certified cell exists; serving it requires net-new OFFLINE saddle rho<1 map training (out of scope). The proposed Leg C (certified w_cert) + construction-time auto-wire were TRIMMED as redundant on the in-scope rho>=1 saddle population and dormant for the connecting region. The connecting region instead gets a hard-assert refusal guard (correctly falls through to the exact engine) — a follow-up build to train the axial map is owed. The image_count==4 deltoid-interior fence is preserved. The census mirror (surrogate_census.py) is re-gated in the same build to keep served-set == counted-set. eta_floor=0.15, tie_eps=1e-12 absolute, and all test tolerances/oracle carry the Professor's authority. Any SPEC.md / DATA_CONTRACTS.yaml mention of the saddle rho floor is doc-staleness for the Librarian doc-sync phase, not a WP.

### WP1: Re-key saddle serve gate onto directional eta + mirror-pair tie discipline
  What: In cogwheel/lensing/likelihood.py, re-key the single-source-of-truth saddle serve gate to serve the transverse cone via a directional nearest-caustic-distance predicate and to treat symmetry-tied mirror pairs as non-resolving. Retire the scalar rho accuracy term from the saddle serve path ONLY. Do NOT touch positive-parity gates, charts, _ppgo_above_ceiling, or the certified-map (_ppgo_cell_coords/_ppgo_band_split) machinery — those are out of scope and stay byte-identical.
  Where: cogwheel/lensing/likelihood.py: `_saddle_farfield_analytic_serves` (~536-590); the live rung `_saddle_farfield_analytic` (~2075-2160); the module constant `_SADDLE_FARFIELD_RHO_FLOOR` (~205); imports (~105-108).
  How: 1) Add module constants `_SADDLE_ETA_FLOOR = 0.15` (Professor-pinned: inside the measured refuse-max 0.05 / admit-min 0.5 gap, ~3x above refuse, biased conservative because a false-admit is a silent lnL bias while a false-refuse only falls back to the exact engine) and `_SADDLE_TIE_EPS = 1e-12` (absolute; mirrors `_airy_fold._CUSP_TIE_EPS` — a symmetry-tied mirror pair has delta_tau at the ~1e-15 machine floor, which is >0 so the current `delta_taus[delta_taus>0]` filter does NOT catch it; absolute not spread-scaled so genuinely-resolvable tight pairs are not falsely swallowed). Document each constant's provenance in a comment. 2) Change the serve gate to accept the directional distance instead of rho. Recommended signature `_saddle_farfield_analytic_serves(real_delays, w_lo, eta)`: Leg A term becomes `if eta is None or not np.isfinite(eta) or eta < _SADDLE_ETA_FLOOR: return False`; Leg B keeps `real = np.sort(...); delta_taus = np.diff(real)` but the surviving gaps are `delta_taus[delta_taus > _SADDLE_TIE_EPS]` (was `> 0`) — if none survive the pair is non-resolving so return False, else `return w_lo * float(np.min(surviving)) >= RHO_END`. Composition is exactly `A AND B`. 3) In the live rung `_saddle_farfield_analytic`, replace the now-dead `rho = caustic_rho(...)` computation in the saddle serve path with `eta = geometry.nearest_caustic_point(lens['gamma'], np.hypot(y1,y2), source, kappa=lens['kappa']).distance` — note `nearest_caustic_point` is invoked ONCE per band-serve (not per w-sample) and the caustic object is already on the critical path (channels.evaluate ~L1977), so this is amortized. If the ChangRefsdalChannels/geometry_partition object already exposes the nearest-caustic result, reuse it rather than recomputing (query the partition first). Pass eta into the serve gate. The image_count==4 deltoid-interior fence must remain: verify the existing path still refuses 4-image interiors (do not weaken it). 4) Remove the now-unused `_SADDLE_FARFIELD_RHO_FLOOR` constant and its docstring IF nothing else in the saddle serve path references it (grep first; if positive-parity code references it, leave it and only stop USING it in the saddle gate). Confirm `caustic_rho` import is still needed elsewhere before removing it. Data-artifact note: this WP touches no registered producer/consumer artifact — the certified_ppgo_map/lens_amplification_surrogate paths are explicitly NOT modified (Leg C trimmed).
  Who: Coder
  Verification: `_saddle_farfield_analytic_serves` gates on directional eta (>= 0.15) for accuracy and on w-resolution with symmetry-tied mirror pairs (delta_tau <= 1e-12) excluded; serve condition is A AND B. The live saddle rung computes eta from nearest_caustic_point (once per band, reusing the partition's caustic object where available) and no longer computes/consults the scalar rho floor in the saddle serve path. The image_count==4 deltoid-interior fence still refuses. Positive-parity gates, the certified-map machinery, and _ppgo_above_ceiling are byte-identical. No new certified-map install or auto-wire logic was added.
  Max turns: 45

### WP2: Re-gate the saddle census mirror onto eta (served == counted)
  What: Update the saddle far-field census classifier in cogwheel/lensing/surrogate_census.py so it computes the SAME directional eta and calls the re-keyed serve gate with identical inputs, preserving the served-set == counted-set invariant. This is a faithful mirror of WP1's live-rung caller — same predicate, same eta computation, same tie discipline.
  Where: cogwheel/lensing/surrogate_census.py: the `if gamma > 1.0:` saddle-farfield mirror block (~490-530) that currently computes `rho = caustic_rho(gamma, np.hypot(y1,y2), kappa=0.0)` and calls `_saddle_farfield_analytic_serves(...)` setting `record.category = 'saddle-farfield-analytic'`.
  How: Replace the census `rho` computation with `eta = geometry.nearest_caustic_point(gamma, np.hypot(y1,y2), source, kappa=<same kappa the live rung uses>).distance` and pass `eta` into the updated `_saddle_farfield_analytic_serves(real_delays, w_lo, eta)` (new signature from WP1). Use the exact same kappa convention as the live rung (WP1) — do NOT hardcode kappa=0.0 if the live rung uses lens['kappa']; mirror the live rung faithfully. Do not introduce a second copy of eta_floor/tie_eps — import/reference the WP1 module constants so there is one authoritative value. The category label and all other census bookkeeping stay unchanged. This is census-only offline classification, so the per-draw nearest_caustic_point call cost is acceptable.
  Who: Foreman-Lite
  Dependencies: WP1
  Verification: The census saddle-farfield block computes eta via nearest_caustic_point (not scalar rho) and calls the re-keyed serve gate with the same signature, kappa convention, and shared eta_floor/tie_eps constants as the live rung; census admit/refuse decisions match the live serve on every witness (served == counted). No duplicated threshold literals.
  Max turns: 20

### Professor Inputs
  - eta_floor = 0.15 (Einstein units): inside the measured refuse-max 0.05 / admit-min 0.5 gap, ~3x above refuse, biased conservative because a false-admit is a silent lnL bias whereas a false-refuse only falls back to the exact engine. Do NOT scale with gamma — nearest-caustic distance is already absolute.
  - Composition is (A AND B) for the serve; the certified-map Leg C is trimmed. §0 finding: the certified ppGO map is keyed on the SAME scalar rho (caustic_rho) and hard-refuses saddle rho<1 cells, so the connecting region (rho<0.5) has NO certified cell — serving it needs offline saddle rho<1 axial-map training and is OUT OF SCOPE. The connecting region ships as a refusal guard; a follow-up build is owed.
  - nearest_caustic_point(...) is invoked ONCE per band-serve (channels.evaluate ~L1977 / geometry_partition ~L2095), NOT per w-sample, and the caustic object is already on the critical path — so directional eta is amortized and the Simplifier's per-sample-cost premise is wrong. The wedge-membership predicate |sin 2(theta-beta)| <= (1-kappa)/|gamma| is REJECTED: it bounds the caustic's angular support (necessary, not sufficient for proximity) and would false-admit angularly-aligned but radially-distant sources — a silent lnL bias. eta (true Euclidean distance) stays.
  - tie_eps = 1e-12, ABSOLUTE (mirror _CUSP_TIE_EPS): symmetry-tied mirror pairs are 0 to machine precision (Fermat-potential x->-x reflection); a spread-relative tolerance would falsely swallow small-but-real resolvable gaps.
  - eta REPLACES rho in the accuracy leg; rho survives only as the certified-map cell coordinate — which is not used in this build since Leg C is trimmed. image_count==4 is the exact interior/exterior fence on both parities (no radius/rho/eta test is equivalent) and must refuse regardless of any other leg.
  - Oracle & bar: validate the analytic serve against f_schwinger reached through the mass-sheet identity, anchored at 2-3 witness points by the independent 2D rotated-contour lens-plane oracle (validated to ~2e-15 on saddles) so the primary oracle is not self-referential; numerical bar is 1e-4 relative on |F| across w<=60 (below the DD_PRODUCT_CEILING of 60). Connecting-region ppGO is ~1e-5..1e-6 at w>=25, giving ~10x headroom IF it were served (it is not this build).

### Domain Test Descriptions
  - T1 — Transverse-cone witness is SERVED (Leg A AND B). Setup: a macro-saddle config (gamma=1.2, kappa=0) with the source on the hard-axis (transverse) cone such that nearest_caustic_point(...).distance (eta) lies in [1.0, 2.5] and the geometry yields exactly 2 real images with a resolvable non-mirror pair (w_lo * min positive delta_tau >= RHO_END=4.0). Operation: call the re-keyed serve gate (must ADMIT — this config was refused under the old rho<2.0 floor), then serve F(w) via the analytic FARFIELD_KERNEL_SUM rung and compare to the saddle oracle (f_schwinger reached through the mass-sheet identity F_{kappa,gamma}=(1/lambda)exp[iw(ln lambda/2 - kappa|y|^2/(2lambda))]F_{0,gamma/lambda}, anchored at 2-3 witness w-values against the independent 2D rotated-contour lens-plane oracle so the primary oracle is not self-referential). Expected: admitted; pointwise |F_served - F_oracle|/|F_oracle| < 1e-4 for every w in [w_lo, 60]. Diagnostic: a rel-error-vs-w curve crossing 1e-4 reveals an eta_floor set too low or a stationary-phase envelope failure near the cusp.
  - T2 — Connecting-region REFUSAL guard (this build does NOT serve it). Setup: a macro-saddle config (gamma>1) with the source on the origin->deltoid symmetry axis at rho<0.5 whose image pair is a symmetry-tied mirror pair (delta_tau <= tie_eps=1e-12) and image_count==2, at w>=25. Operation: call the re-keyed serve gate. Expected: it REFUSES (returns False) — Leg B excludes the tied pair as non-resolving and there is no certified saddle rho<1 cell to admit it — so the config correctly falls through to the exact engine. This is the honest current state; the test documents that the connecting region is deferred to a future offline-map build. Diagnostic: if the gate ever ADMITS this config, an eta or resolution leg has been mis-composed and would emit a wrong (unserved) value.
  - T3 — Deltoid-lobe interior REFUSES (image_count==4 fence). Setup: a macro-saddle source placed strictly inside a deltoid lobe so the geometry yields exactly 4 real images (geom.real_mask.sum()==4), the genuine diffractive caustic interior. Operation: call the re-keyed serve gate (and, if reachable, the live rung dispatch). Expected: refuses on all legs regardless of eta or w — real-image count 4 is the exact interior discriminator and FARFIELD_KERNEL_SUM is O(1)-wrong there. Diagnostic: an admit here would inject a grossly wrong |F|; assert refusal explicitly.
  - T4 — Mirror-pair non-resolving has teeth (tie_eps discipline). Setup: (a) an on-axis saddle source whose only pair is symmetry-tied (delta_tau <= tie_eps) with no other resolvable positive gap -> Leg B must return False even at large w; (b) perturb the SAME source slightly off the symmetry axis so delta_tau > tie_eps and the pair becomes genuinely resolvable at the band floor -> Leg B flips to True (only the tie changes; eta held above floor and w fixed). Expected: (a) refuse, (b) admit. Diagnostic: if (a) admits, the delta_taus filter is still using `>0` instead of `> tie_eps`; if (b) refuses, tie_eps is too large and is swallowing real gaps.
